(Policy Objectives) Tj
0 -14 Td
(-----------------) Tj
0 -14 Td
(Transport and infrastructure policy seeks to improve connectivity, reduce logistics costs,) Tj
0 -14 Td
(increase safety and support economic activity. Roads, railways, airports, ports, waterways) Tj
0 -14 Td
(and urban transport form an interconnected system.) Tj
0 -14 Td
() Tj
0 -14 Td
(Integrated Planning) Tj
0 -14 Td
(-------------------) Tj
0 -14 Td
(PM GatiShakti is associated with integrated infrastructure planning and coordination. The) Tj
0 -14 Td
(objective of integrated planning is to reduce duplication and improve connections between) Tj
0 -14 Td
(different transport and infrastructure networks.) Tj
0 -14 Td
() Tj
0 -14 Td
(National Logistics Policy) Tj
0 -14 Td
(-------------------------) Tj
0 -14 Td
(The National Logistics Policy focuses on improving the efficiency of moving goods. Logistics) Tj
0 -14 Td
(performance is affected by infrastructure, regulation, warehousing, digital systems,) Tj
0 -14 Td
(last-mile connectivity and coordination among agencies.) Tj
0 -14 Td
() Tj
0 -14 Td
(Roads and Highways) Tj
0 -14 Td
(------------------) Tj
0 -14 Td
(Highway development can reduce travel times and improve market access. Policy must also) Tj
0 -14 Td
(address maintenance, road safety, land acquisition, environmental impacts and the connection) Tj
0 -14 Td
(of highways to local roads.) Tj
0 -14 Td
() Tj
0 -14 Td
(Railways and Public Transport) Tj
0 -14 Td
(-----------------------------) Tj
0 -14 Td
(Railways support both passenger and freight movement. Urban transport policies also address) Tj
0 -14 Td
(metros, buses and multimodal systems. Investment decisions must consider demand,) Tj
0 -14 Td
(affordability and long-term operating requirements.) Tj
0 -14 Td
() Tj
0 -14 Td
(Ports and Aviation) Tj
0 -14 Td
(------------------) Tj
0 -14 Td
(Ports and airports connect domestic and international markets. Their effectiveness depends) Tj
0 -14 Td
(not only on terminals but also on surrounding roads, rail links, customs processes,) Tj
0 -14 Td
(warehousing and other supporting infrastructure.) Tj
0 -14 Td
() Tj
0 -14 Td
(Project Progress and Performance) Tj
0 -14 Td
(--------------------------------) Tj
0 -14 Td
(Transport projects pass through approval, land acquisition, contracting,) Tj
0 -14 Td
(construction and commissioning stages. A length awarded to a contractor is not) Tj
0 -14 Td
(the same as a length completed or opened to traffic. Similarly, reduced travel) Tj
0 -14 Td
(time, lower freight cost, fewer accidents and higher passenger volume are) Tj
0 -14 Td
(different outcomes. A logistics corridor can improve freight movement while a) Tj
0 -14 Td
(nearby village still lacks a last-mile connection. Claims about project success) Tj
0 -14 Td
(should name the stage, route, mode and measurement period.) Tj
0 -14 Td
ET
